{"module":"channel_breakout","rationale":"Single-symbol channel breakout. The channel is the highest and lowest close of the `lookback` bars before the current one; the current bar is excluded. When the latest close breaks above the high, the strategy targets +units. When it breaks below the low, it targets -units, or flat when long_only is set. Inside the channel it keeps its current position. The channel length is a bounded integer parameter `lookback` (2 to 250, default 20). Orders are the signed change from the current position, so they are deterministic and keep no state across bars. On attempt 1 the contract check rejected the template description; it is now a short literal well under 400 characters.","source":"from finquint.backtesting import MarketOrder
from finquint.strategies.base import Param, StrategyTemplate


class ChannelBreakoutStrategy:
    def __init__(self, symbol, lookback=20, units=5000, long_only=False):
        self.symbol = symbol
        self.lookback = int(lookback)
        self.units = units
        self.long_only = bool(long_only)

    def on_bar(self, context):
        history = context.history
        if history is None or len(history) == 0:
            return ()
        rows = history[history["symbol"] == self.symbol]
        closes = rows.sort_values("timestamp", kind="mergesort")["close"].dropna()
        n = self.lookback
        if len(closes) < n + 1:
            return ()
        window = closes.iloc[-(n + 1):-1]
        upper = float(window.max())
        lower = float(window.min())
        last = float(closes.iloc[-1])
        current = context.positions.get(self.symbol, 0)
        if last > upper:
            target = self.units
        elif last < lower:
            if self.long_only:
                target = 0
            else:
                target = -self.units
        else:
            return ()
        change = target - current
        if change == 0:
            return ()
        order_id = "channel_breakout-" + str(self.symbol) + "-" + str(context.timestamp)
        return (MarketOrder(order_id, self.symbol, change, context.timestamp),)


TEMPLATE = StrategyTemplate(
    "channel_breakout",
    "Channel breakout on one symbol: target +units when the close rises above the highest close of the previous `lookback` bars, and -units (or flat when long_only) when it falls below the lowest close of the previous `lookback` bars; otherwise keep the current position.",
    {
        "lookback": Param("integer", 2, 250, 20),
        "units": Param("number", 1, 10000, 5000),
        "long_only": Param("boolean", default=False),
    },
    ChannelBreakoutStrategy,
)
"}
